{
  "description": "Cross-stack fingerprint contract for codeguardFingerprint/v1. src/scanner/baseline.ts (TypeScript) and src/ai_code_audit/fingerprint.py (Python, also used by the Opengrep backend) must produce exactly these values. tests/unit/fingerprint-contract.test.ts and tests/test_fingerprint_contract.py each read this file. The purpose of the field layout is to remove concatenation ambiguity between fields; a 64-bit truncated digest is not collision-free and is not claimed to be.",
  "key": "codeguardFingerprint/v1",
  "baselineVersion": 1,
  "spec": {
    "fields": "rule id, then path, then snippet, joined by U+0000 (NUL). File paths cannot contain NUL and rule ids do not use it (custom rule ids are unconstrained strings, so this is a convention there, not a guarantee); with NUL absent from the first two fields the split is unambiguous (see vectors field-shift-a / field-shift-b).",
    "ruleId": "Used verbatim and case-sensitively. TypeScript: Finding.ruleId. Python: metadata.rule_id, else finding.id, else \"unknown\".",
    "path": "Every U+005C (backslash) is replaced by U+002F (slash); nothing else is changed. TypeScript: Finding.file, which the orchestrator already makes cwd-relative with forward slashes. Python: metadata.relative_path (repository-relative), else finding.host. The two agree when the TypeScript CLI runs from the repository root.",
    "snippet": "TypeScript: Finding.snippet. Python adapter only: metadata.snippet, else the last evidence entry, else description, else title; after normalisation a leading \"sink line N: \" / \"source line N: \" evidence prefix is removed. Cross-stack vectors below exercise the shared core, not the Python-only source selection.",
    "whitespace": "Each maximal run of the canonicalWhitespace code points becomes one U+0020, then leading and trailing U+0020 are removed. The set is fixed here on purpose: JavaScript \\s and Python \\s differ (JS-only U+FEFF; Python-only U+001C-U+001F and U+0085) and both depend on the engine's Unicode version.",
    "encoding": "UTF-8. An unpaired surrogate is encoded as U+FFFD (Node's behaviour; Python previously raised UnicodeEncodeError).",
    "digest": "SHA-256, lowercase hex, first 16 characters (64 bits)."
  },
  "canonicalWhitespace": [
